From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ROG5 Linux Project <rog5-linux@localhost>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] phy: qcom: qmp-ufs: stop SM8350 diagnostic after regulators

Generation 34 proved that loading and registering the QMP-UFS driver is safe
when its platform device cannot bind.  For the next RAM-only discriminator,
allow the exact SM8350 device to bind, acquire its clocks and regulator
handles, apply the existing reviewed regulator loads, then return before DT
MMIO parsing, clock-provider registration, PHY creation, or PHY-provider
registration.

This diagnostic-only patch cannot initialize the PHY or expose UFS storage.

Signed-off-by: ROG5 Linux Project <rog5-linux@localhost>
---
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-ufs.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-ufs.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-ufs.c
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-ufs.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-ufs.c
@@ -2223,6 +2223,13 @@ static int qmp_ufs_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	if (of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node,
+				    "qcom,sm8350-qmp-ufs-phy")) {
+		dev_notice(dev,
+			   "ROG5 QMP-UFS diagnostic: regulator stage complete\n");
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	/* Check for legacy binding with child node. */
 	np = of_get_next_available_child(dev->of_node, NULL);
 	if (np) {
-- 
